{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/15157-unfleshed-bestowments-transmutations","id":15157,"title":"Unfleshed Bestowments & Transmutations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T22:59:18-08:00","id":15157,"title":"Unfleshed Bestowments & Transmutations","content":"I have at least one player who is planning on playing an Unfleshed in my upcoming Promethean game and wants the power to briefly give sentience and animate electronic devices. As I was talking with him about this I was trying to figure out if this made more sense as a Bestowment or if the Unfleshed's relationship with technology was so entrenched that it would require a new Transmutation to really completely flesh it out. I don't have the answer to that but I was curious what other people have done in their campaigns. For this player in particular I am considering giving him a unique Bestowment to animate electronic devices and then creating a Transmutation for Unfleshed that more generally discussed their interactions with technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:53:10-08:00","id":15214,"title":"","content":"Considering the zeka can animate zombies as their bestowment, an electronic version hardly seems out of bounds to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:13:32-08:00","id":15564,"title":"","content":"...So there's already a Vulcanus Transmutation for this.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly what you're looking for,as it doesn't grant sentience, but close enough - Animate Firetouched. Page...156.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T18:01:04-08:00","id":26160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/15157-unfleshed-bestowments-transmutations?p=15564#post15564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...So there's already a Vulcanus Transmutation for this.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly what you're looking for,as it doesn't grant sentience, but close enough - Animate Firetouched. Page...156.</div> </div> </div> </div>The player has been very specific that he wants his character to create objects that have sentience not just control an object. The idea would be that the character has a difficult time with these objects because he longs for them to be permanent and act as companions to him even though they are, by nature, transient. Here is something I have cooked up for him. The idea behind Animate Inanimate is that Jed imbues a bit of self-consciousness into a technological invention. Given that Jed was created to be a companion we could understand this Bestowment as a kind of \u201crussian doll\u201d type of power where Jed (designed to be a companion himself) can create a lesser companion himself (the object affected by Animate Inanimate).<br /> <br /> <b>Animate Inanimate</b> (Unfleshed)<br /> <br /> Unfleshed who are created primarily to be companions to humanity have sometimes been constructed with the ability to raise up companions of their own. Progenitors of these Unfleshed hoped that they might alleviate mankind\u2019s existential loneliness, unknowingly adding to the alienation that Unfleshed with this Bestowment must feel when they imbue their incomplete progeny with life.<br /> <br /> <i>Cost:</i> 3 Pyros<br /> <br /> <i>Action:</i> Simple<br /> <br /> <i>Transmutation Cost:</i> ?<br /> <br /> <i>Dice Pool:</i> Azoth + Computers<br /> <br /> When the Promethean uses this ability he names an Aspiration and a personality trait and chooses one mechanical object within sight.<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure:</i> The mechanical object is brought to life with an Aspiration and personality trait twisted and opposite from that the Unfleshed expected. If there is no interesting opposite to the Aspiration named by the Unfleshed the object instead becomes a Gremlin.<br /> <br /> <i>Failure:</i> The Pyros is spent but the mechanical object fails to achieve sentience. Additional rolls for this Bestowment on this object suffer a -1 penalty. This is cumulative.<br /> <br /> <i>Success:</i> The object comes to life and seeks to complete its Aspiration. For dice pools relevant to its functioning it uses the Promethean\u2019s Azoth + 3. For other dice pools it uses only the Promethean\u2019s Azoth. If the mechanical device would be unable to accomplish a given task it cannot roll. At the dawn of each day the Promethean must spend 1 Pyros if he wishes the object to continue to benefit from this Bestowment. Once the object has completed its Aspiration it loses its sentience. This Bestowment may be used on the same object again but will never completely replicate the same being twice.<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Success:</i> As success save that when the object completes its Aspiration the Promethean may immediately spend 3 Pyros to give it a new Aspiration and an additional personality trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T18:39:27-08:00","id":26187,"title":"","content":"I'd make it so a Dramatic Failure is <i>always</i> a Gremlin, usually with a twisted version of the aspiration. I'd also close any loopholes for indefinite duration by making deliberate attempts or overly-vague wordings automatically create a Gremlin ('Help me find Humanity.' 'Make me happy.' 'Be my friend, forever' - I am evil, sometimes) and specify that you can only have one active at a time (Gremlins obviously not counting towards the limit).<br /> <br /> What's the logic for things moving round? Does the animated gun extrude metal strut-limbs? Does the laptop unfold like a tiny Transformer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:46:07-08:00","id":26635,"title":"","content":"Well, using the GMC rules dramatic failure is now a choice, correct? I would be worried that the Bestowment could be abused to factory farm Pandorans by a Centimani if it always produced Gremlins. Perhaps that whole element should be reconsidered actually. Not necessarily removed but carefully considered. As for open-ended Aspirations, I am actually happy enough for a Promethean to give those since it costs him a Pyros per day to keep the thing up and running. You are right that a clause about only having one at a time is necessary. I prefer that objects only be able to do what they are physically capable of already. I should sit down with the player and find out if he agrees because the Bestowment is ultimately for his use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T13:49:50-08:00","id":26711,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't worry about players being able to choose to fail dramatically because firstly, this can only be done once per scene and secondly, developers have clarified that players should not be allowed to help their characters by choosing dramatic failures (as it is still a failure). Especially Demon: the Descent gets absurdly broken otherwise.<br /> <br /> Developer quotes about Demon:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11909#post11909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No storyteller should allow this. Some embeds have absurdly broken powers if allowed to deliberately fail. Plus it's kinda against the spirit of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=13950#post13950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can choose to dramatically fail a roll <i>if you failed the roll to begin with</i>. But if you're using the power, my assumption as ST is that you're trying to do what the Embed actually does. Want to do the dramatic failure effect more consistently? Fine, teach yourself to do it (that is, make up a new Embed or Exploit).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> EDIT: I really like the bestowment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:53:41-08:00","id":26859,"title":"","content":"Someone already mentioned &quot;Animate Firetouched.&quot; Doesn't &quot;Imaginary Friend&quot; do the other half?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:00:07-08:00","id":26900,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does; and they\u2019re explicitly designed to work together.<br /> <br /> Frankly, when I read the subject line of this topic what immediately came to mind was the notion of Transmutations and Bestowments designed primarily to interact with technology. Something that lets you hear and transmit radio signals, for instance; or to tell at a glance how a machine is malfunctioning. Such a set of Transmutations could easily be split up among the existing sets (e.g., radio signals could fall under Sensorium, while manipulating machinery might fall under Alchemus; and a lot of Electrification is usable in this manner as is); and in fact it would be interesting to compose tech-oriented \u201cextensions\u201d to as many of the existing sets as possible for use by the Unfleshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:56:10-08:00","id":26935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/15157-unfleshed-bestowments-transmutations?p=26859#post26859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone already mentioned &quot;Animate Firetouched.&quot; Doesn't &quot;Imaginary Friend&quot; do the other half?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez. Really wish I'd seen that in my first pass through after my player and I discussed this ability.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think I have an issue with combining the two powers, limiting them to work on electronic objects, and making it an Unfleshed Bestowment. Hijacking lesser devices seems well within the Unfleshed shtick and, as StSword pointed out, the Zeka already have the Re-animator Bestowment which could also theoretically be handled with Imaginal Friend + Animate Firetouched. I really appreciate you pointing out Imaginal Friend, however, as it gives me a better framework for developing the final version of the Bestowment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:57:47-08:00","id":26936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/15157-unfleshed-bestowments-transmutations?p=26900#post26900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, when I read the subject line of this topic what immediately came to mind was the notion of Transmutations and Bestowments designed primarily to interact with technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like this idea! Basically the thread is supposed to be an open call for developing Transmutation / Bestowment resources for Unfleshed characters so anything in that vein is within bounds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}